  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for Hawaii's 1st Congressional District features an August 8 Democratic primary in which incumbent Rep. Ed Case (D) faces a progressive challenge from state Sen. Jarrett Keohokalole and several other candidates. Case, a moderate Democrat first elected in 2018 who previously served in the House from 2002 to 2007, has drawn criticism from within his party for occasionally voting with Republicans. The district, covering urban Oahu including Honolulu, is rated Solid/Safe Democratic by all major forecasters (Cook Political Report, Inside Elections, Sabato's Crystal Ball), meaning the Democratic nominee is heavily favored in the November 3 general election. State Rep. Della Au Belatti had been a prominent primary challenger but withdrew to run for lieutenant governor shortly before the filing deadline.",
